            <ArticleTitle>Absent infrarenal inferior vena cava.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>535</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2484/rcr.v6i3.535</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Absence of an infrarenal inferior vena cava is an infrequent finding on computed tomography scans and is usually an unexpected, incidental finding. This report concerns a young patient with an absent infrarenal inferior vena cava who presented with abdominal and back pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
